  "description": "Independence rules. Everything is a { value, label } pair: value is the stable key used by logic and stored data and never changes; label is the text people see and can be renamed freely. Treatments and relationships are defined once below and rules refer to them by value. A relationship's phrase is the plain-language wording used in the independence decision. Each rule lists entries; each entry is one treatment, the relationships (measured from an audit client) it applies to, and exemptServiceLines: the service lines exempt from that treatment for those relationships (it can be empty). A relationship appears in at most one entry per rule, so use separate entries of the same treatment to give relationships different exemptions. This file starts from the config embedded in the wizard. The wizard does not use service lines yet, so exemptServiceLines is not read and its embedded copy has not been updated.",

  "serviceLinesNote": "Values in exemptServiceLines are service line values such as TAX-101; a value ending in * is a prefix match, so TAX* is every TAX- service line. Nothing reads them yet.",

